<title>USA: 46 million watched Dole-Clinton debate - Nielsen.</title>
<headline>46 million watched Dole-Clinton debate - Nielsen.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The televised debate between Republican Bob Dole and President Bill Clinton drew 46.1 million viewers, 34 percent fewer than watched a comparable 1992 debate, Nielsen Media Research said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The total was derived from all those who watched Sunday's debate on ABC, CBS, NBC, CNN and Fox networks, the television ratings firm said.</p>
<p>At a comparable presidential debate in 1992, the second in a series of three, 69.9 million people watched.</p>
<p>The first debate in 1992 was not comparable to this campaign season's first matchup because in 1992, CBS declined to carry the debate so it could broadcast a baseball playoff game.</p>
</text>
